          %p
            Before we start, beware the usual terminology issue with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoids"}> simplicial groupoids
            ”:
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (terminology)
              This entry is concernd with
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoids"} simplicial groupoids
              as traditionally understood (following
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer &amp; Kan (1984)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              with the special property that their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              of objects is simplicially constant. Any such “Dwyer-Kan simplicial groupoid” is equivalently an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+category"} sSet-enriched category
              that is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched
              sense: an
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"}> sSet
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+groupoid"} enriched groupoid
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              which matters, a more accurate term would be
              = succeed "," do
                %em simplicially enriched groupoids
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicial groupoid
              (
              %a{:href => "simplicial+groupoid#Definition"}> here
              ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
