                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0 = \ast
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+groupoid"} terminal groupoid
              is, when regarded as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of the)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              which is its unique
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoids"} delooping groupoids
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeMorphismsOfSimplicialGroupoids"}
              are those of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+groups"} model structure on simplicial groups
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ExtraModelCategoryProperties Extra model category properties
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                  %mtext -
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet\text{-}Grpd
            for the category of Dwyer-Kan simplicial groupoids.
          %p
          #SimplicialIntervalGroupoid.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (simplicial interval groupoid)
              %br/
              Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi sSet
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ℐ
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    sSet
                    \\overset{\mathcal{I}}{\longrightarrow}
                    sSet\text{-}Cat
                    \\longrightarrow
                    sSet\text{-}Grpd
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+groupoid"} enriched groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}(S)
              which has precisely two objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0,1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
              and isomorphisms between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              freely generated from the cells of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          This is
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan84"} Dwyer &amp; Kan (1984), §2.8
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor+construction"} Milnor construction
          in
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine09"} Goerss &amp; Jardine (2009), pp. 314
          %a{:href => "#Bergner08"} Bergner (2008), p. 4
          the statement of free generation is missing.)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The construction of Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialIntervalGroupoid"}
              applied to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[0]
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-simplex"}> 0-simplex
              , “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"}> singleton
              ”) is the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+groupoid"} interval groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇆
                      %mo ∼
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\ast) \,=\,
                    \\big\{
                    0 \overset{\sim}{\leftrightarrows} 1
                    \\big\}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The model structure on simplicial groupoids from Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheModelStructure"}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
              with generating (acyclic) cofibrations the images under the simplicial interval functor (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialIntervalGroupoid"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#AsACofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"} there
              = succeed "-" do
