                    %use{:x => "139.037858", "xlink:href" => "#kgEKllsaTv9ZlxPksei-P9YWlnY=-glyph6-2", :y => "74.968905"}
              Regarded this way as a diagram in the slice, the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \sslash G) \times_{\mathbf{B}G} (-)
              preserves its retraction property.
            %p
              Therefore it is sufficient to prove the claim under the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{f}
              is actually a free map.
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \subset Mor(\mathbf{Y})
              denote a
              %a{:href => "#SetOfFreeGenerators"} set of generators
              which exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{f}
              as a free map. We claim that then the set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (W \sslash G)
                    \\times_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\Gamma
                    \\;\;
                    \\subset
                    \\;\;
                    Mor\big(
                    (W \sslash G)
                    \\times_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\mathbf{Y}
                    \\big)
            %p
              serves as a set of generators exhibiting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \sslash G) \times_{\mathbf{B}G} f
              as a free map, and hence as a cofibration.
            %p
              Namely, by the nature of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \sslash G) \times_{\mathbf{B}G} \mathbf{Y}
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big( p_{\mathbf{Y}}(\phi), \phi \big)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (w, y) \longrightarrow (w', y')
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' \,=\, p_{\mathbf{Y}}(\phi) \cdot w
              is determined by the pair consisting of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon y \to y'
              and of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Obj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in Obj(\mathbf{Y})
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              has a unique reduced decomposition into
              = succeed "-components" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⫽
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \sslash G)\times_{\mathbf{B}G} \Gamma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              With the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#AssumptionForFiberProductWithActionOneGroupoid"} above assumptions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+category"} slice model category
              of the DK-model structure:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi Map
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi W
                          %mo ⫽
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi W
                          %mo ⫽
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sSet\text{-}Grpd_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\underoverset
                    {
                    \\underset{
                    Map\big( W \sslash G, - \big)_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    }{\longleftarrow}
                    }
                    {
                    \\overset{
                    (W \sslash G)
                    \\times_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    (-)
                    }{\longrightarrow}
                    }
                    { \bot_{\mathrlap{Qu}} }
                    sSet\text{-}Grpd_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              With Lem.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberProductWithActionOneGroupoidPreservesCofibrations"}
              it is now sufficient to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \sslash G) \times_{\mathbf{B}G}(-)
              preserves all weak equivalences.
            %p So assume that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{f}_{x,x'}
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\mathbf{X}(x,x')
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbf{Y}\big(\mathbf{f}(x),\mathbf{f}(x')\big)
            %p
              is a weak equivalence for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ,
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi Obj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w,w' \,\in\, Obj(\mathbf{X})
            %p
              By the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{f}
              is a map in the slice over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+unions"} disjoint unions
              indexed by
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{f}_{x,x'}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{g \in G}{\coprod}
                    \\Big(
                    \\mathbf{f}^g_{x,x'}
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\big((p_{\mathbf{X}})_{x,x'}\big)^{-1}
                    \\big(\{g\}\big)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\big(
                    (p_{\mathbf{Y}})_{
                    \\mathbf{f}(x),
                    \\mathbf{f}(x')
                    }\big)^{-1}
                    \\big(\{g\}\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Accordingly, all the components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{f}^g_{x,x'}
              must be weak equivalences. But then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi w
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi w
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi G
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi w
                          %mo =
                          %mi w
                          %mo ′
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (W \sslash G)
                    \\times_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\mathbf{f}
                    \\big)_{(w,x), (w',x') }
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{
                    {g \in G}
                    \\atop
                    g \cdot w = w'
                    }{\coprod}
                    \\mathbf{f}^g_{x,x'}
            %p is a coproduct of weak equivalences and hence a weak equivalence.
